  "updated_at": "2026-10-18T22:35:33Z",
  "body": "Thanks, `ERR_NETWORK_CHANGED` was it, and it isn't a builder bug: I've reported it to Vitest as vitest-dev/vitest#11636.\n\nStarting a container changes the host's IP addresses, and Chromium then aborts module requests in flight to the dev server. In the stalled runs, all of them were Vitest's and Vite's own modules, and there was no 504. When one of the tester's modules fails to load, Vitest waits out the 60 s iframe timeout instead of failing. Failing one of those requests on purpose stalls plain Vitest the same way, with or without `isolate`, and that's the reproduction in the Vitest issue. Angular's testers load more modules, so they get caught more often, which is why plain Vitest looked unaffected next to a container. `ng test --isolate` stalls as well, in 1 run of 10.\n\nOne correction to my report: the builder sets its own Playwright provider when `browsers` is set, so the Chromium flags I passed through `runnerConfig` never reached the browser. The \"no failed request\" check and the \"full Chromium\" runs didn't test what they said.\n\nClosing this in favour of the Vitest issue.\n",
